show with animations:
   if (coding is slow but fun):
       you can prompt with code
       a pseudocode line types itself, the margin mark goes from needs-a-build to built, and real code slides in underneath

   when code gets complicated:
      abstractions get created for you
      three settled lines fold into a named box and leave a one-line reference behind
   when agents have questions:
      they build their best guess and show you the other way
      the other way appears right on the line, the person switches to it and passes, the agent builds that one

      "Underpaint" font: rounder felt-marker hand (Patrick Hand), upright and easy to read small, shipped with the site

      let's use building a tic tac toe as an example for the landing.
          one game across the scenes: click(cell) gets built, winner(board) folds into a box, restart() offers X-first or loser-first
      make pseudocode mroe like code, less like prose.
      for psedocode in different style in (python-like, js/c-like, clojure-like) {
          show that agent adapts and follows style
